    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1068">

                <pb facs="1102" n="1088" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1088"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00/1238a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d1068-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-03T18:00:00-04:00">April 3, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>201. You are requested to discuss the subject matter of the Department’s
                    preceding telegram<anchor n="7" xml:id="d1068-f2"/> with your military, naval
                    and legal attachés, if available, and to request them very discreetly to note
                    whether there is any movement of arms or forces which indicate any intention of
                    interfering in any way in the Salvadoran revolutionary disturbance.</p>
                <pb facs="1103" n="1089" xml:id="pg1089"/>
                <p>Please report to the Department any significant information pertaining to the
                        above.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d1068-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1068-f1" n="6" type="source" xml:id="d1068-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated as telegrams Nos. 156 to Nicaragua and 87 to Honduras.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1068-f2" n="7" xml:id="d1068-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 200, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1068-f3" n="8" xml:id="d1068-f3-content">
                <p>Replies from Guatemala, Nicaragua, and Honduras (telegrams Nos. 217, 215, and 102
                    of April 4, respectively), reported no indications of interference; telegrams
                    not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
